# Build context is the repo root (`docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .`), so this
# file must live HERE, not in docker/.
#
# Allow-list style: exclude everything, then re-add only what the Dockerfile
# COPYs or bind-mounts. The image carries NO repository code (jobs ship it as a
# code_source snapshot), so no code or doc edit can reach -- or bust -- the build.
# A new COPY must be added here too, or the build fails at once with
# "failed to compute cache key: not found".
*

# extra CA bundles for corporate TLS interception (`make certs`; .gitkeep by default)
!certs
!certs/**
# `make vendor` output, bind-mounted (never COPYed) and checked against the locks
!vendor
!vendor/**
!docker
docker/*
# the retry wrapper used by every network step, and uv with the build's index
!docker/retry.sh
!docker/uvi.sh
# the pins: Python constraints + the non-index artefacts (sha256 / commit)
!docker/requirements.lock
!docker/artifacts.lock
# compile-only probe for the FlashInfer/CCCL toolchain check (Dockerfile step 5c).
# Kept as a real file because escaping a multi-line .cu through
# Dockerfile -> /bin/sh -> printf mangled the #include directives.
!docker/cccl_probe.cu
